---
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title={`Privacy & cookie choices — ${SITE_NAME}`} description={`How ${SITE_NAME} handles analytics, advertising preferences, local browser storage and contact reports.`} path="/privacy/"><section class="container section-block"><div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Your choices</p><h1>Privacy and cookies</h1></div><div class="prose"><h2>Reading this site</h2><p>You can read the guides without creating an account. Our hosting provider processes technical request information needed to deliver pages, such as IP addresses and browser request details, under its own service arrangements.</p><h2>Analytics</h2><p>If analytics is configured and you choose to allow it, we use Google Analytics to understand page use and improve our guides. Optional measurement includes searches, reading depth and transitions between guides. We do not send typed search terms, contact details or other form contents as analytics events. Analytics is not loaded before your choice.</p><h2>Advertising</h2><p>If advertising is configured and you allow advertising storage, a configured advertising provider may use cookies or similar technologies. Additional regional consent requirements must be met before those services are enabled. See our <a href="/advertising/">advertising disclosure</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">Google's explanation of partner-site data use</a>.</p><h2>Your browser preferences</h2><p>We store your consent choices in your browser so the site can remember them. You can reopen privacy choices from the footer. Withdrawing consent stops further optional measurement and reloads the page to remove already loaded optional services. You can also remove site data through your browser settings.</p><h2>Contact and correction reports</h2><p>Our public issue tracker is operated by GitHub under its privacy policy. Public reports are visible to others; do not submit private travel, payment or identity details. If an email address is provided on our contact page, correspondence is used to respond to the enquiry.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for privacy questions or correction requests.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
